WEBVTT

00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:18,100
First of all, is there specific hormonal support for somebody on their monthly cycles but has heavy cycles?

00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:24,100
So hormonal support with somebody with heavy cycles, you want to look at...

00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:30,100
First of all, anybody's having any type of hormonal issues. It's best to get tested.

00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:44,100
So doing a Dutch test, which is a dried urine hormone test, is the best approach to get all your estrogen and progesterone testosterone numbers checked.

00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:49,100
Because there's all these intermediate metabolites that you want to look at.

00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:55,100
If you're having issues with cycles, if you're having issues with getting pregnant, if you're having any type of hormonal...

00:00:55,100 --> 00:01:02,100
Anything you think that is hormonally based, I'm not talking about your thyroid, because that should be a separate test.

00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:14,100
But the Dutch test is the way to go. Getting a Dutch test to look at the balance of all those intermediate estrogens and progesterones and androgens.

00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:22,100
And the Dutch test also gives you an adrenal cortisol profile. That's the thing to get checked first.

00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:34,100
So before you go into manipulating your hormones that are being careful, anything that you take that's hormonally driven, it isn't just supporting like a nutrition that's supporting the glands.

00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:41,100
If you're doing something that is hormonally itself, all your hormones work on a negative feedback loop.

00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:50,100
So if you're taking DHA, that works on a negative feedback loop, but that will basically shut down production of DHA in the adrenal glands.

00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:55,100
It's a common supplement that's out there that's used by a lot of practitioners, people with adrenal fatigue.

00:01:55,100 --> 00:02:01,100
But you've got to be careful taking that because that will shut down your adrenal glands.

00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:06,100
So the best thing to do, whatever you're having, any hormonal issues get tested.

00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:13,100
Thyroid tests, so your thyroid doesn't specifically control your estrogen and progesterone.

00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:17,100
It's a good idea to get that checked on everybody on a regular basis anyhow.

00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:21,100
So if you're in one of our courses, do our complete wellness panel.

00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:31,100
That gives you a complete bit of all the profile and a complete CDC with differential, some other things that I like to look at.

00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:37,100
That can point to different health patterns and it gives you a complete thyroid profile.

00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:42,100
So a complete thyroid profile, remember, is not just your TSH, T3 and T4.

00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:54,100
It's T3, T4, T3, T3, T4, reverse T3, TSH, thyroid, globular antibodies and TPO antibodies.

00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:59,100
So you want to look at that whole big picture when you look at your thyroid plate.

